# **Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.**
#
# Added the day the third CI leg arrived (2026-08-14). Git's default on Windows
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, and this repository is full of files whose
# bytes are the test: `tests/golden/**/*.expected` is compared byte for byte, the
# double-emit determinism check hashes generated C, and `printer::gallery` asserts
# every example is in canonical form. A checkout that changed the bytes would make
# a third of the suite fail on one platform for a reason that is not in any of the
# programs.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises in the repository and checks out unchanged, so all
# three legs read the same bytes the author wrote.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# A case whose bytes ARE its CRLF line ends (defect 135's L2, 2026-10-02): a
# literal left open at `\r\n`. Normalised to LF it would test nothing, so git
# keeps it as written, on every leg.
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-135-l2-*.hero -text

# And an `f"…"` literal left open at `\r\n` (defect 135's open CRLF site,
# lane recovery-b7, 2026-10-02), with what `check --apply` writes of it.
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-135-crlf-*.hero -text
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-135-crlf-*.applied -text

# A message at a CRLF line end told where an LF line end is (defect 373,
# lane cli12, 2026-10-06): its bytes are its CRLF line ends.
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-373-*.hero -text
